REFERENCE   1  (bases 1 to 5326)
  AUTHORS   Zhang,D., Efendic,S., Brismar,K. and Gu,H.F.
  TITLE     Effects of MCF2L2, ADIPOQ and SOX2 genetic polymorphisms on the
            development of nephropathy in type 1 Diabetes Mellitus
  JOURNAL   BMC Med Genet 11, 116 (2010)
   PUBMED   20667095
  REMARK    GeneRIF: MCF2L2 Leu359Ile polymorphism is associated with decreased
            risk of diabetic nephropathy in female type 1 diabetes mellitus.
            GeneRIF: Observational study of gene-disease association and
            gene-gene interaction. (HuGE Navigator)
REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 5326)
  AUTHORS   Zheng,Q., Shi,Y., Yang,Z., Xu,X., Wang,L., Xue,F., Gu,H.F. and
            Chen,Z.J.
  TITLE     Family-based association study of the MCF2L2 gene and polycystic
            ovary syndrome
  JOURNAL   Gynecol Obstet Invest 68 (3), 171-173 (2009)
   PUBMED   19648752
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Results suggest that the genetic polymorphisms within
            MCF2L2 may confer an increased susceptibility to PCOS in the
            Chinese population. Data may provide a basis for further studies of
            the role of the MCF2L2 gene in the etiology of PCOS.
            GeneRIF: Observational study of gene-disease association. (HuGE
            Navigator)
