COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from AC093422.3, BC060870.1 and
            AY429674.1.
            This sequence is a reference standard in the RefSeqGene project.
            
            On Nov 23, 2018 this sequence version replaced NM_015375.2.
            
            Summary: This gene encodes a dual serine/threonine and tyrosine
            protein kinase which is expressed in multiple tissues. It is
            thought to function as a regulator of cell death. Multiple
            transcript variants encoding different isoforms have been found for
            this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Dec 2008].
            
            Transcript Variant: This variant (1) encodes the longer isoform
            (1).
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
