            Al-Futaisi,A., Al-Maawali,A. and Alkuraya,F.S.
  TITLE     Recessive mutations in SCYL2 cause a novel syndromic form of
            arthrogryposis in humans
  JOURNAL   Hum Genet 139 (4), 513-519 (2020)
   PUBMED   31960134
  REMARK    GeneRIF: results suggest that severe neurogenic arthrogryposis with
            brain malformation is the human phenotypic consequence of SCYL2
            loss of function mutations.
REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 5977)
  AUTHORS   Miyakawa,K., Sawasaki,T., Matsunaga,S., Tokarev,A., Quinn,G.,
            Kimura,H., Nomaguchi,M., Adachi,A., Yamamoto,N., Guatelli,J. and
            Ryo,A.
  TITLE     Interferon-induced SCYL2 limits release of HIV-1 by triggering
            PP2A-mediated dephosphorylation of the viral protein Vpu
  JOURNAL   Sci Signal 5 (245), ra73 (2012)
   PUBMED   23047923
  REMARK    GeneRIF: results suggest that SCYL2 serves as a regulatory factor
            for Vpu, reducing the extent of Vpu phosphorylation and
            consequently enhancing BST2-mediated viral restriction.
REFERENCE   3  (bases 1 to 5977)
