COMMENT     VALIDATED REFSEQ: This record has undergone validation or
            preliminary review. The reference sequence was derived from
            DB481173.1, AK002148.1 and BC010847.1.
            
            On Nov 23, 2018 this sequence version replaced NM_018381.3.
            
            Summary: This gene is an interferon stimulated gene (ISG) that
            inhibits viral replication. The encoded protein binds nucleic acids
            and inhibits programmed -1 ribosomal frameshifting required for
            translation by many RNA viruses. Viruses inhibited by the protein
            include Zika virus, dengue virus and the coronaviruses, SARS-CoV
            and SARS-CoV2. [provided by RefSeq, Aug 2021].
            
            Transcript Variant: This variant (1) represents the longer
            transcript and encodes the longer isoform (1).
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
